<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coptic Orthodox Church</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Coptic Church</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Coptic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a> is the main Christian church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, headed by the Pope of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>. It rejected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-chalcedon">Council of Chalcedon</a> in 451 and became separate from the imperial church, and most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> followed it until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> gradually spread after the Arab conquest. It also consecrated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Christian Nubian kingdoms such as Makuria, and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coptic-orthodox-church.jpg" alt="Coptic Orthodox Church" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland Unger · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CairoAbbasiyaMarkEntrance.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
